{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gnarled-wraithlike-flatfish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAt audited code snapshot `9a94ef9737fbdf070ae314bba6e797319aee2301`,\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py:166-352`\n`_compute_outbound_update_mutation` accepts 24 loose values spanning remote observation,\ntransport, binding state, mapping policy, diagnostics, and mutation output. Related field-diff seams\naccept 14 and 11 values at\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_field_diff.py:235-475`.\n\nBrant's typed-payload stories make mutation outputs discriminated by direction/action, but output\ntyping alone does not guarantee that producer construction stops threading the current loose\ndependency bundle. Adding another mapping axis, sink, collaborator, or policy otherwise continues\nto require synchronized edits across builder, caller, and helper boundaries.\n\nProvenance: janitor finding A04 (validity 1.00, impact 0.92), discovered during\n`literal-subaverage-dartfrog`. Commit `52d9e5f34ea3` extracted the builder for module headroom but\ndid not decide its input ownership.\n\n## Approach / End State\n\n- Start from the accepted contract and typed payload union produced by\n  `scummy-ultrashort-tuatara` and `earthborn-statuelike-boutu`.\n- Re-census the current producer and successor seams after the typed implementation lands. If the\n  cited 24-value seam has already been eliminated, record the evidence and do not create substitute\n  work.\n- Otherwise divide construction along the existing observation-resolution, canonical-diff,\n  comment/label/link assembly, and typed-mutation construction seams so each stage receives only\n  the data and collaborators it owns.\n- Reuse RP-03's `Observation` / `TicketPlan`, Brant's payload contracts, and existing runtime\n  bindings. A small typed request is acceptable only when its fields form one cohesive invariant;\n  do not wrap the same loose bundle in a generic context, option bag, or\n  `Mapping[str, Any]`.\n- Keep production on the pre-cutover route in this story. `single-vast-roan` remains the owner of\n  production flip and legacy-dispatch deletion.\n\n`cascade_flag=true`: census callers, string imports, monkeypatch targets, compatibility re-exports,\nstandalone file loading, manifests, and Cloud/DC adapter projections before changing the seam.\n\n## Sequencing\n\nThis story starts after `earthborn-statuelike-boutu` lands the types and portable parity oracle.\nIt must close before `single-vast-roan` flips production and deletes the legacy route.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse Brant's portable synthetic/scrubbed replay corpus as the main behavior oracle. Existing\nCloud/DC verified-fake contracts, mutation tests, effect spies, deterministic traces, module-size,\ncomplexity, lint, and typecheck gates remain green. No live Jira or production dual-send is needed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A post-`earthborn-statuelike-boutu` census records the surviving mutation producers,\n      callers, dynamic consumers, and the disposition of the cited 24/14/11-value seams.\n- [ ] No surviving production or shadow mutation producer retains the current 24-value loose bundle\n      or merely hides it inside a generic context, option bag, or `Mapping[str, Any]`.\n- [ ] Observation resolution, canonical diff, ancillary-operation assembly, and typed mutation\n      construction each receive only cohesive owned inputs; Brant/RP-03 domain types are reused\n      rather than duplicated.\n- [ ] Retry, idempotency, fuse, and transport-resource ownership remain exactly where ADR 0103 and\n      the existing runtime seams place them; no second owner is introduced.\n- [ ] The portable legacy/typed corpus has zero unexplained trace or modeled-state deltas, and effect\n      spies prove this story adds no production write route or dual-send path.\n- [ ] Semantic and string/dynamic-reference censuses find no stale supported import, monkeypatch,\n      manifest, or adapter consumer after the change.\n- [ ] Focused reconciler suites, verified Cloud/DC fake contracts, module-size and complexity gates,\n      lint, and typecheck pass without weakened assertions.\n- [ ] Production cutover and legacy deletion remain unimplemented here and explicitly owned by\n      `single-vast-roan`.","id":"6452-715f-21c9-4285","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["architecture","reconciler","typed-payload","maintainability","janitor"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Converge typed mutation producers onto cohesive construction inputs"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788055323325550278,"uuid":"cbb553f1-98c1-4234-a6bd-e737a0852bcf"}